### Findings (Part 3)
- With ALB + auto scaling, the system sustains higher load without large latency spikes.
- ECS scales out when CPU utilization stays above the target for the cooldown period.
- Load is distributed across healthy targets; stopping a task does not bring down the service.
- Horizontal scaling provides resilience and improved performance compared to a single task.

